{
  "id": "ss.relic.giant",
  "name": "Giant instar",
  "description": "One amber body swollen until it fills the plate \u2014 it stands to the panel's inner edge on the top, right and bottom with nothing between it and the rim, and stops there \u2014 with three segment bands curving across it and a highlight up on the shoulder. Down in the free lower-left corner sits a body of the ordinary size, a pale oval with one band, there to be the ruler. Half again the body, more health and more area is a relic about being large, so the icon is mostly not-plate. No eyes, no legs, no face: it is a mass with segments and not an animal looking at you. Fit pass: the outline used to cross onto the gold, which read as too-big on the page and did not survive the game \u2014 the rim is the two outer pixels `BootScene.makeRelicGradeIcons` repaints with the find's grade, so what crossed was flattened to a grade colour and the glyph cutout lost it as well. Filling the panel to its edge says the same thing and keeps it.",
